      },
      "text": {
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown",
        "initialization": "",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "source": "",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "WebServerApp — the routes of the WebServer example, served by the WebServer component\n(examples/webserver-component.orch) placed here as the Reference `http`.\n\n`http.request` feeds the router; every route answers into `http.response`. The router,\nthe routes and the response bodies belong to this design; accepting, rendering, writing,\nlogging and freeing belong to the component (see its root Specification).\n\nROUTES\n| Method   | Path          | Status | Content-Type                  | Entity              |\n| GET/HEAD | /home/about   | 200    | text/plain; charset=utf-8     | routeHomeAbout      |\n| GET/HEAD | /home/version | 200    | text/plain; charset=utf-8     | routeHomeVersion    |\n| GET/HEAD | /api/user     | 200    | application/json              | routeApiUserDetails |\n| other    | known path    | 405 (+ Allow: GET, HEAD)                | routeNotFound       |\n| any      | unknown path  | 404                                     | routeNotFound       |\n| —        | unparsable request line | 400                           | routeNotFound       |\nThe query string is ignored for matching. HEAD returns the GET header without a body.\nEvery response carries Content-Type, Content-Length, Connection: close and Server.\n",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "Build: compile with wirecraft.compile_c17 into a new directory, then\n  clang -std=c17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic WebServer.c -o webserver\nRun: WEBSERVER_PORT=18080 WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=6 ./webserver\nExpect (curl -s -i):\n1. GET /home/about   → 200, text/plain, body names the example.\n2. GET /home/version → 200, text/plain, body \"WebServer 0.1.0 (Wirecraft C17)\".\n3. GET /api/user?x=1 → 200, application/json, valid JSON with \"name\":\"Ada Lovelace\".\n4. GET /missing      → 404, body \"404 Not Found: /missing\".\n5. POST /home/about  → 405 with \"Allow: GET, HEAD\".\n6. HEAD /home/about  → 200 header with Content-Length of the GET body and no body.\nAfter the sixth request the process exits 0 and has printed six access-log lines.\n",
        "testsLanguageId": "json"
      },
      "typeDefinition": null
    },
